Other adjustments

We want to add a line with intercept the US rate.
Lets compute that


r &lt;- murders |&gt; 
  summarize(rate = sum(total) /  sum(population) * 10^6) |&gt; 
  pull(rate)

Quadratic discriminant analysis

With these estimates in place, all we need are the prevalence \(\pi\) to compute:

\[
\widehat{p}(\mathbf{x})= \frac{\widehat{f}_{\mathbf{X}|Y = 1}(\mathbf{x}) \widehat{\pi}}
{ \widehat{f}_{\mathbf{X}|Y = 0}(x)(1-\widehat{\pi}) + \widehat{f}_{\mathbf{X}|Y = 1}(\mathbf{x})\widehat{\pi} }
\]

Balanced accuracy and \(F_1\) score

Because it is easier to write, you often see this harmonic average rewritten as:

\[
2 \times \frac{\mbox{precision} \cdot \mbox{recall}}
{\mbox{precision} + \mbox{recall}}
\]

